comments.body:
@hawkinsp I would be tempted to say that we don't have to guarantee any consistency there, so long as we don't have a crash bug maybe.  (I.e. I think the only annoyance is thread-sanitizer reporting it correctly.)

I.e. setting `writable` on an array like that (that you are not uniquely owning) seems very dubious either way.

The original flags updating reported here seems just a defensive artifact of the past that can be removed -- i.e. the update should be doing nothing, but I think thread-sanitizer will still report it? (Contiguity flags should always be set correctly on all arrays and never change -- there were historical 10+ years outdated reasons for them being updated).
